data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc`'d `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** Both work as expected:

```csharp
Span<nint> span = stackalloc nint[5];
Span<nuint> uspan = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

On this 64-bit system, `nint` is 8 bytes. The native-sized integer types (`nint`/`nuint`, available since C# 9) are valid `stackalloc` element types just like any other unmanaged type.
